==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtraɪfəl/}}
* {{audio|en-us-trifle.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|aɪfəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# An [[English]] [[dessert]] made from a [[mixture]] of thick [[custard]], [[fruit]], [[sponge cake]], [[jelly]] and [[whipped cream]].
# An [[insignificant]] [[amount]].
# Anything that is of little importance or worth.
# A particular kind of [[pewter]].
# {{uncountable}} [[utensil]]s made from this particular kind of pewter.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|insignificant amount}} [[iota]], [[jot]], [[scrap]], [[whit]]
* {{sense|thing of little importance or worth}} [[bagatelle]], minor detail, [[whiffle]]

====Derived terms====
* [[a trifle]]<!--adverb: somewhat-->

